    "reflectionAnalysis": "Azure error XML may describe invalid request fields. In this exact invocation those fields are service-issued URL components, fixed headers, decimal lengths, generated IDs and block-list structure; opaque artifact contents are not reflected by the documented Put Block/Put Block List contract. Changing payload size may influence response choice, but does not select arbitrary XML entity syntax. No repository bytes enter the URL/query or XML BlockList. This is source/contract analysis, not a claim to inspect private Azure implementation.",
    "trustBoundary": [
      "manual dispatch only",
      "trusted tool checkout separated from data checkout",
      "contents:read",
      "no PR/pull_request_target trigger",
      "no ordinary secret input",
      "six artifact basenames",
      "no repository script execution or repository-controlled upload endpoint in frozen invocation"
    ],
    "maliciousInputAlternatives": [
      "Compromised/misbehaving Azure upload endpoint returns malicious XML",
      "Compromised/misbehaving GitHub artifact service returns attacker endpoint or insecure signed URL",
      "Compromised trusted runner/proxy/CA/TLS configuration permits authenticated response substitution",
      "Another trusted-infrastructure failure that supplies malicious service XML"
    ],
    "transportQualification": "SDK allowInsecureConnection:true permits a service-supplied HTTP URL; no local hostname allowlist is enforced. Frozen workflow does not select endpoint or disable TLS validation. Normal signed endpoint is HTTPS. Redirect policy defaults to same-origin (cross-origin and HTTPS-to-HTTP changes rejected); PUT follows eligible 300/307 only under trusted response. Thus this is hosted infrastructure trust, not a universal HTTP/TLS or host-pinning guarantee.",
    "serviceResponseScope": "XML is exclusively consumed from the selected hosted upload service response on this path; it is not exclusively Azure if GitHub changes the returned endpoint. A malicious chosen XML requires trusted-service/endpoint or transport failure, but a benign Azure error reaches the parser without compromise."
  },
  "mitigation": {
    "entityLimit": "PARTIALLY_BOUNDS_DIFFERENT_ENTITY_PATH; DOES_NOT_PREVENT_THIS_ADVISORY",
    "entityLimitExplanation": "1000 caps DOCTYPE-defined substitutions, but standard/numeric-alias loops bypass accounting. 1001 witness proves property violation, not a workflow DoS.",
    "htmlEntitiesFalse": "PARTIAL: disables general numeric/HTML table, leaves standard and numeric-alias substitutions uncounted. Maintainer workaround is not a complete mitigation for exact 5.4.1.",
    "xmlValidation": "UNRELATED_TO_RESOURCE_LIMIT: accepts well-formed repeated entities",
    "frozenBoundary": "Prevents repository contributors from choosing vulnerable service-response XML; selected disposition is attacker-control classification, not a claim that parser is mitigated."
  },
